WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.200
Data security is everybody's business.&nbsp;
There are a number of security solutions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:10.080
out there. There are a number of security&nbsp;
products driving these security solutions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:13.200
And certainly, the security&nbsp;
teams are always inundated with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:18.000
too many alerts, too many products,&nbsp;
and too many solutions to keep up with.&nbsp;

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:31.200
Data security is a constantly evolving and&nbsp;
a moving target. So when we talk about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:37.920
challenges of data security, it's all about having&nbsp;
an understanding of what data an organization has,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:43.120
understand what are some of the compliance&nbsp;
mandates the organization needs to comply with.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:48.400
And more importantly, be able to get to a&nbsp;
more proactive state where organizations are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:55.840
managing and remediating security threats as they&nbsp;
arise. And that's really where Zero Trust light&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.840 --> 00:01:02.480
frameworks come into picture. Zero Trust ensures&nbsp;
that you are verifying everything and not really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:09.360
banking on trusting anything without verification.
Privacy and data security and governance are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:14.480
interrelated. They are two phases&nbsp;
of the same coin in the sense that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:20.960
privacy is something that you could drive with&nbsp;
having a robust data governance process and having&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:27.680
a very solid framework to enforce data governance&nbsp;
from a security point of view. And that's really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:33.520
where data security solutions come in to play.
IBM believes the current state of data security&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:40.880
can be improved. We believe the market from here&nbsp;
goes towards more of an open and interconnected&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:46.800
space where security solutions could talk to&nbsp;
each other and essentially enable security&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:54.880
orchestration and response in a more congenial and&nbsp;
more homogenous way. And IBM Security solutions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.880 --> 00:02:00.880
are built using some of the security first&nbsp;
principles like separation of duties, being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:06.800
able to deliver data-centric security controls&nbsp;
and ultimately drive all this in a way that is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:14.640
enabling security teams to manage data security&nbsp;
threats and prioritize actions and remediation.&nbsp;

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:19.760
What that provides is the ability&nbsp;
for organizations to have their teams&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:25.360
across the board from compliance to privacy,&nbsp;
from risk management to applications,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:31.280
infrastructure to operations, all come together&nbsp;
to address business challenges and particularly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:37.360
data security threats and events in a more&nbsp;
collaborative way. My name is Rajesh Venkatasubbu,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:49.840
product manager at IBM Security, and responsible&nbsp;
for data security and guardian data protection.

